# Supply-chain hardening (card t_546aa53b, Google GTIG guidance).
# - ignore-scripts: no package lifecycle script runs on install. Verified safe:
#   the only hasInstallScript entry in package-lock.json is fsevents
#   (macOS-only optional dep, unused on Linux CI), and `npm run build`
#   passes with scripts disabled (Vite 8 needs no postinstall build step).
# - min-release-age=1: install only versions published >1 day ago (unit is
#   DAYS; verified: a 2-day-old release resolves under =1 and is excluded
#   under =3). Requires npm 11+ — CI pins npm@11.19.1 before install; older
#   npm ignores the key. Emergency override per package:
#   min-release-age-exclude=<name> (use sparingly, with a dated comment).
ignore-scripts=true
min-release-age=1
